    "reply": "The variant record for rs334 lists several clinical significance classifications but names no specific associated condition, so these findings do not show what condition rs334 is linked to [1]. The literature search returned one HGVS-style variant name and several other rsIDs [2]. The retrieved findings do not describe the variant itself.\n\n## Clinical Significance\n\nThe recorded clinical significance values are not-provided, protective, likely-benign, pathogenic, other [1]. Submitters have given conflicting interpretations, ranging from benign-leaning and protective to pathogenic [1]. Because no disease or phenotype is attached to these classifications in the findings, the associated condition cannot be stated from this evidence [1].\n\n## Literature Variant Names\n\nThe literature search returned the variant name c.20A>T [2]. It also returned the variant name c.-50T>C [5]. The findings do not say whether either name refers to rs334 itself [2].\n\n## Other Returned Identifiers\n\nThe search also returned rs334348 [3]. It returned rs334353 as well [4]. It also returned rs334773 [6]. These are distinct rsIDs that start with the same digits as rs334, so they should not be read as evidence about rs334 without separate confirmation [3].",
    "dur": 12.813
   }
